Portions adapted from MailCraft

WhatSpace follows the setup and conventions of MailCraft (https://github.com/billsecond/mailcraft),
and these parts started from MailCraft's source, which is Copyright (c) 2026 the MailCraft
contributors and licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0 (MailCraft's
NOTICE says which of them in turn started from WordCraft, https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft,
Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team and the WordCraft contributors, under the same licences):

- workspace tooling: xtask (layers, assets, ci, stats, version, ico, the icon renderer's
  supersampling), rustfmt and clippy settings, the lint set;
- packaging scripts and metadata for macOS, Windows, Linux and FreeBSD (packaging/), and the
  release workflows (.github/workflows/), which call the shared craft-common-actions;
- the Windows graphics-backend choice (apps/whatspace/src/graphics.rs).

The squarified treemap layout follows the published algorithm of Mark Bruls, Kees Huizing and
Jarke J. van Wijk, "Squarified Treemaps" (2000).
